@@@!atrep

@@/ at-djot: a syntax mapper for a useful subset of Djot. The
@@/ sim inventory deliberately mirrors at-markdown one-for-one
@@/ under djot's own symbols (emphasis _underscores_, strong
@@/ *stars*), so the pair is connected by a std isomorphism -
@@/ the graph's first lossless edge. Code maps to the core
@@/ enlexis forms.

@=== heading-1
@# grammata #@
@"level-1 heading; flat, does not nest content"@
===@

@=== link
@>< grammata ><@
@"hyperlink; the grammata is the displayed URL"@
===@

@=== heading-2
@## grammata ##@
@"level-2 heading"@
===@

@=== heading-3
@### grammata ###@
@"level-3 heading"@
===@

@=== heading-4
@#### grammata ####@
@"level-4 heading"@
===@

@=== heading-5
@##### grammata #####@
@"level-5 heading"@
===@

@=== heading-6
@###### grammata ######@
@"level-6 heading"@
===@

@=== emphasis
@_ grammata _@
@"emphasis (_underscores_)"@
===@

@=== strong
@* grammata *@
@"strong emphasis (*stars*)"@
===@

@=== blockquote
@>
grammata
>@
@"block quotation (> prefix)"@
===@

@=== unordered-item
@-
grammata
-@
@"bullet list item (- marker); items form flat runs"@
===@

@=== ordered-item
@.(taxis)
grammata
.@
@"enumerated list item (N. marker); items form flat runs"@
===@

@@/ The footnote extension ([^label] references, [^label]:
@@/ definitions): the koine construction, shared symbol with
@@/ at-markdown.

@=== footnote
@^
grammata
^@
@"footnote body ([^label]: text); attached by deixis callouts"@
===@
